    <!-- Help View Strings -->
    <system:String x:Key="TitleHelp">System User Guide</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="TitleHelpTopics">Topics</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpSubtitle">A comprehensive guide to help you navigate and use all system features effectively</system:String>
    
    <!-- Help Topics -->
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicIntroTitle">1. Introduction</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicIntroContent">Welcome to the Sources System.&#xA;&#xA;This system is designed to seamlessly manage and track radioactive sources. Using this guide, you will learn how to navigate the system, manage inventory, handle borrowing requests, and generate comprehensive reports.&#xA;&#xA;Use the sidebar on the right to navigate between different system modules. The top bar contains your notifications bell and the ability to collapse the sidebar for more screen space.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicDashboardTitle">2. Dashboard</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicDashboardContent">The Dashboard provides a high-level overview of the entire system.&#xA;&#xA;Key Features:&#xA;• KPI Cards: Displays the total number of sources, active vs. stored breakdown, and total current activity.&#xA;• Recent Alerts: Highlights items requiring immediate attention (e.g., sources with low activity after 6 half-lives or overdue returns).&#xA;• Activity Charts: Visualizes the distribution of source activities over time and by isotope.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicRadioisotopesTitle">3. Radioisotopes</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicRadioisotopesContent">The Radioisotopes module allows you to manage the types of radioactive materials used in your facility.&#xA;&#xA;Features:&#xA;• Add New: Click 'Add Isotope', enter the symbol (e.g., Cs-137), atomic number, mass number, and half-life.&#xA;• Edit/Delete: Use the action buttons next to each isotope in the list to modify or remove records.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicSourcesTitle">4. Sources Inventory</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicSourcesContent">The core of the Sources system. Here you track all physical radioactive sources.&#xA;&#xA;Adding a Source:&#xA;1. Navigate to the Sources section and click 'Add Source'.&#xA;2. Fill in the required fields: Source Code, Isotope, Initial Activity and its Unit, Manufacturer, and Location.&#xA;3. The system automatically calculates the Current Activity based on the isotope's half-life.&#xA;&#xA;Managing Sources:&#xA;• Use the 'Edit' button to update details like Status (Active, Stored, Disposed).&#xA;• View complete tracking history by clicking on the source details.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicBorrowingTitle">5. Borrowing System</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicBorrowingContent">Manage the checkout and return of radioactive sources.&#xA;&#xA;Creating a Request:&#xA;• Go to the Borrowing section and click 'New Request'.&#xA;• Select the source, the borrower's name, the purpose of use, and the expected return date.&#xA;&#xA;Approvals &amp; Returns:&#xA;• Supervisors can 'Approve' or 'Reject' pending requests.&#xA;• Once a source is returned, it must be marked as 'Returned' to update the primary inventory status.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicReportsTitle">6. Analytics &amp; Reports</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicReportsContent">Generate official documents summarizing system data.&#xA;&#xA;Available Reports:&#xA;• General Report: A comprehensive report combining all data below.&#xA;• Inventory Report: Full list of all registered sources.&#xA;• Borrowing Report: History of all source checkouts and returns.&#xA;• Low Activity Alerts: Lists sources that have decayed significantly or passed 6 half-lives.&#xA;&#xA;Exporting:&#xA;Click the PDF or Excel buttons at the top of the screen to download the currently viewed report.</system:String>

    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicSettingsTitle">7. Settings &amp; Users</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="HelpTopicSettingsContent">System Administration and Configuration.&#xA;&#xA;User Management:&#xA;• Create new accounts and assign roles (Admin, Supervisor, User).&#xA;• Roles determine which sections of the application are accessible.&#xA;&#xA;System Settings:&#xA;• Backup &amp; Restore database ensuring data integrity.&#xA;• Toggle Application Theme (Light/Dark mode) and Language.</system:String>

